{
  "version": "1.0",
  "name": "Tutorial 10: Demoscene - Neural Shaders",
  "description": "Drive GLSL shaders with neural network signals!\n\nTHE DEMOSCENE:\nIn the 80s/90s, hackers made stunning visuals on\nlimited hardware. Plasma, tunnels, fractals - all\ndriven by math functions like sine and time.\n\nNOW YOU CAN TOO:\n1. TIME node outputs elapsed seconds\n2. SINE transforms time into smooth oscillation\n3. NOISE adds organic randomness\n4. SHADER_VIS renders GLSL with your signals!\n\nTHE ARCHITECTURE:\n- Time drives the animation\n- Sine creates smooth waves\n- Multiply combines signals\n- Shader receives values as 'uniforms'\n\nTRY THIS:\n1. Watch the shader animate automatically\n2. Adjust SINE frequency for faster/slower waves\n3. Change NOISE scale for more chaos\n4. Edit the shader code in the Inspector!\n\nThis is how neural networks can drive generative art.",
  "metadata": {
    "created": "2025-12-19T22:00:00",
    "modified": "2025-12-19T22:00:00",
    "author": "Noodlings Tutorial",
    "total_parameters": 0
  },
